; regression test locking in an invariant `new_var_name`/`new_bool_var_name` (kurt.py)
; rely on: fresh internal names use a doubled prefix (`$$01`, `%%01`, ...) "because the
; `$$` ensures that it is not a kurt variable that the user can define" (see the comment
; there, and dev/todo-claude.md's (in git history) now-corrected note). This was never actually verified --
; checked here directly: the lexer's SYMBOL pattern is `[$%@]?[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*`, at
; most *one* leading `$`/`%`/`@` followed immediately by a letter -- except `$$x` (todo 35, a
; polymorphic variable, a *letter* after the `$$`), so a doubled prefix followed by digits
; can never be scanned as a symbol at all; it fails at the lexer with a `ScanError`
; before parsing/matching even begins. Confirmed for both `$$` and `%%`; a user can never
; construct a name that collides with a generated one (`$$01`: digits only, a user's `$$x`
; starts with a letter), by construction, not just convention.
expect "ScanError"
    var $$01
expect "ScanError"
    prop %%foo
true

